  - "decision, step 2: GEMM2 = materialised fp16 hidden in L2 (written before sync 2) + split-K over a (c-slice x k-split) CTA grid with KS 2-8, red.add volume M*C*4*KS = 2.4-9.6 MB (1-2.5 us). The red.add-of-on-chip-hidden path (KS = 4C/BN = 32-128) would be 38 MB at 2,768. No extra grid sync either way [INFERRED from probe numbers]"
  - "smem: fully resident fp32 W1+W2 slices fit only where M <= ~400 at C=768 (BN=24 -> 74 KB each). 16/32,768 need ntile >= 4 and weight streaming, which makes the design weight-streaming per slice rather than weight-stationary. Final smem 114-205 KB per CTA [INFERRED from planner]"
  - "v1 (fp32 W fragments converted by every warp at fragment load; rolled GELU epilogue) run_tests 16/16, us: 2,768 49.8; 8,768 99.1; 16,768 123.6; 32,768 217.8; 8,384 74.3; 16,384 130.2 [run_tests]"
  - "v1 stamps at 32,768 (CTA medians, us): A done 13.3, sync1 14.8, G1 pass0 mainloop 57.1, G1 done 132.6, sync2 135.2, C prologue 140.5, G2 mainloop 211.7, end 218.4. No-MMA ablation 97.7 us vs 222 full [probe_b200]"
  - "v2 (W chunk converted once per chunk into fp16 smem, B fragments via ldmatrix) gained only 5-15%. Ablation at 32,768: full 232 / no compute 101 / no compute + no W TMA 98 / no compute + no A bulk 96 / no compute + no loads 92 us. So neither the bytes (W strided 128-B TMA rows are fine) nor the MMA set the time; the kernel's skeleton does [probe_b200]"
  - "root cause (per-chunk globaltimer stamps): latency-bound smem loops at 16 warps/SM with no ILP. (a) LN-stats prologue after sync1: 24 __ldcg per token issued one after another under '#pragma unroll 8' with a runtime count, 5 us at 2,768 and 7-9 us at 32,768. (b) Rolled warp-per-row GELU epilogue: 16.6 us per G1 pass at 32,768 (2.3 at 2,768), the same pathology as lineage B's 16 us epilogue. (c) W conversion loop with a runtime trip count: 1.05 us/chunk in G2 at 32,768 (4 per-image copies). (d) Bare chunk skeleton (wait + 2 __syncthreads + refill): 0.26 us/chunk = 25 us over 96 chunks at 32,768 [probe_b200]"
  - "v3 fix: compile-time trip counts with all loads issued before use (LN stats, gf for the GRN scale, W conversion in batches of 3), and 2 rows x HWp/32 tokens of GELU per lane in flight. run_tests 16/16, rented us: 2,768 34.1; 8,768 63.9; 16,768 93.6; 32,768 169.6; 8,384 53.5; 16,384 93.7; other 10 rows = r0 anchor within 3% [run_tests]"
  - "per-chunk compute (v2 stamps at 32,768): mma.sync about 0.64 us per 32-k chunk at 384 HMMA/SM against a 0.40 us ideal. G1+G2 = 96 chunks, so 32,768 floors near 60-70 us with this engine before conv (10 us), syncs and epilogues. 32,768 cannot reach the 75 us target on mma.sync with 128 CTAs plus per-chunk __syncthreads [probe_b200]"
  - "conv phase A (bulk 32-plane groups, thread per 7-output row segment): 1.5 us at 2,768, 6 us at 8,768, 10 us at 32,768 (6 units/CTA), 8-9 us at 8/16,384 [probe_b200]"
  - "precision (fp64 reference, harness-like generators, 1 seed per row, probe): max |err| 1.52-1.84e-3, below the smallest atol 2.4e-3. Single roundings only: d16, fp16(lnw*W1), h16, fp16(s_img*W2), with LN folded as rs*(acc - mu*s1) + c1 and the gb term exact in fp32. Per-row beyond-atol counts over the 10 seeded harness rounds were NOT logged; run_tests passes 16/16 [probe_b200, run_tests]"
  - "verdict H25: refuted as stated. 2,768 met (34.1 <= 35); 8,768 63.9 > 45; 16,768 93.6 > 55; 32,768 169.6 > 75; 8,384 53.5 > 45; 16,384 93.7 > 60. The refutation clause fires at 8,768 (not 10 us faster than A r2 63.1, cross-session). The binding term is not weight ingest or post-sync rounds (stub 17-32 us); it is per-chunk SM time: mma.sync plus a sync-heavy 32-k ring at 16 warps/SM [run_tests, probe_b200]"
  - "value: as a dispatch specialist on 2,768 and 8,384 only (A elsewhere) worth roughly +0.013 of mean (closes about 80% and 60% of those rows' gaps to the leader-implied 27/37 us), short of the +0.03 success line [INFERRED from ledger notes]"
  - "next levers if D continues: KC=64 chunks or a double-buffered fp16 B to halve the per-chunk __syncthreads (about 0.13 us x 48-96 chunks); tcgen05 for 16/32,768 (MMA-bound); stats from an earlier round to drop the 2 us LN prologue at 2,768 [INFERRED]"
